# wifi.env — build-time Wi-Fi networks for switch-board.sh
#
# Copy to `wifi.env` (gitignored) and fill in your known networks. Every
# switch-board.sh setup/build/flash regenerates main/wifi_networks.local.h
# from this file; WifiBoard seeds the networks into NVS on boot, so a
# freshly flashed device joins without a serial `!wifi` step.
#
# This file is PARSED, never executed. Values are taken verbatim to end of
# line; one surrounding pair of quotes is stripped. Keys must not have spaces.
#
# Primary network (WIFI_SSID / WIFI_PASSWORD env vars override these):
WIFI_SSID=MyNetwork
WIFI_PASSWORD=super secret passphrase
#
# Additional networks, WIFI_SSID_2..8 / WIFI_PASSWORD_2..8:
# WIFI_SSID_2=MyNetwork-5G
# WIFI_PASSWORD_2=super secret passphrase
